{# Single-shot markdown artifact submission contract. Single source of truth
   so the prose cannot drift between commit_message, development_analysis,
   review, worker_developer, etc.

   Designed for cheap / small / "dumb" agents that follow numbered steps
   and pattern-match examples. Failure modes the macro defuses: wrong
   artifact_type alias, JSON payloads instead of markdown, wrong section
   headings or item syntax, prose echo, and ambiguous final actions.

   A required artifact receipt and the durable declare_complete sentinel are
   independent evidence. Both are mandatory; stopping after submit caused a
   production retry hang and must remain impossible to misread here.

   ``example_doc`` is a complete example markdown document, typically
   built at the call site with {% set example_doc %}...{% endset %}.
   ``verify_tool_reference`` is optional because some renderers (commit,
   reviewer, worker) do not expose the verify tool.
#}
{% macro render_artifact_submission(artifact_type, submit_tool_reference, example_doc, write_file_tool_reference='', verify_tool_reference='') -%}
## Submit a `{{ artifact_type }}` artifact

Complete all five steps.

1. **Read the format doc** at `.agent/artifact-formats/{{ artifact_type }}.md`
   (or `artifact_formats_index.md`). Do not guess the grammar.

2. **Author the artifact as ONE markdown document**: a `---`-delimited
   frontmatter block (`key: value` lines), then `## Section` headings whose
   content is stable-ID list items of the form `- [ID] text` (one line per
   item) when the format doc defines sections. Example for `{{ artifact_type }}`:

   ```markdown
{{ example_doc | trim | indent(3, true) }}
   ```

3. **Persist the document.** Call {{ submit_tool_reference }} with two
   arguments: `artifact_type` set to `"{{ artifact_type }}"` and `content`
   set to the complete markdown document from step 2 (the full markdown
   text as a plain string — never JSON).
{%- if verify_tool_reference %}
   Optionally call {{ verify_tool_reference }} first with the same two
   arguments to validate without persisting.
{%- endif %}
{% if write_file_tool_reference %}
   If the submit tool does not exist, write the same complete markdown
   document to `.agent/tmp/{{ artifact_type }}.md` via
   {{ write_file_tool_reference }}. Then continue immediately to step 5. The
   completion gate validates and promotes the fallback after that final call;
   it completes the phase only when both the sentinel and promoted receipt exist.
{% endif %}

4. **Wait for a valid durable receipt.** For a submit-tool result with
   `valid: false`, each diagnostic carries a line number, section, and rule
   code — fix every reported line and resubmit ONCE with all repairs applied.
   A direct-submit receipt proves acceptance; the receipt is not phase completion. For a write-file
   fallback, step 5 triggers the completion gate that validates and promotes it.

5. **MANDATORY FINAL ACTION: You MUST call {{ DECLARE_COMPLETE_TOOL_REFERENCE }} as your explicit final action.**
   This writes the separate durable completion sentinel. For a write-file
   fallback, make this call immediately after writing the complete document;
   the runtime then validates and promotes it. Do not stop until the call succeeds.

   Optional `summary` param. Example:
   `{{ DECLARE_COMPLETE_TOOL_NAME }}(summary="{{ artifact_type }}")`.

Use the canonical type and raw markdown text—never JSON—and persist before the explicit completion action.
{%- endmacro %}
